  "findings": [
    "Initial migration creates file metadata, duplicate groups and legacy relation table. The type/hash index and later path_hash index are nonunique. No database unique constraint for duplicate-group(type,hash) or file identity(path_hash,owner) appears in these seven migrations. This supports a missing database-enforced invariant, not a reproduced concurrent insertion failure.",
    "Size starts integer and migrates to BIGINT; file-hash remains a nullable string length200. No algorithm-version or stable physical-file identity column in this schema. Application currently requests SHA256; different hash algorithms were not executed.",
    "Path starts text, becomes string length4000, and gains nullable40-character SHA1 path_hash plus index. Migration only creates column/index; backfill is the separately reviewed repair step. No all-platform path-length or transactional upgrade claim.",
    "Owner becomes nullable. Ignored is added nullable with defaultfalse plus index. Existing FileInfoMapper.findByHash filters ignored=false, so deliberately null ignored values would be excluded; defaulted migration behavior on actual backend remains untested. No ordinary upgrade data-loss claim.",
    "No migration drops file_hash or rewrites its values in the read code. This is source evidence only, not proof that all original records survive actual SQLite/MySQL/PostgreSQL upgrades or interruption.",
    "AbstractFileInfoEvent carries mutable FileInfo plus optional user ID, with no old-content/hash snapshot. New/Updated event subclasses add no fields. This is consistent with the prior listener invalidation concern, not a new runtime reproduction.",
    "Typed exception wrappers preserve messages and, for UnableToParseException, previousThrowable. They do not by themselves supply scan-level completeness; continue to distinguish logged errors from explicit incomplete reports.",
    "PageController and admin settings classes select templates/labels/icons. Annotation comments treated solely as source data; no security settings modified, app installed or user files touched.",
    "All lib/ blobs have now been individually whole-read and Git-blob verified across audits. COPYING, frontend/bundles, packaging, assets, workflows and remaining tests still prevent full repository credit. No local implementation change or performance claim."
  ]
